    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-4419",
      "problem": "Using a cofactor expansion along the $2$nd column, write the following determinant as a combination of $3 \\times 3$ determinants:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14251298/assets/d9a077c7ed79e43564b4379507cf2291d39ba727a8ca5c4180d6038a792d09a0.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Using a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{12}+3\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{42} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14251298/assets/13a7aaf86747e1e64f992cab2fa6267d12231b4da41e1524434333423224ee1a.svg)",
